1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,000
NEW NATIONAL STADIUM
EXPLOSION INCIDENT

2
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,130
The New National Stadium
suffered major damage...

3
00:00:04,130 --> 00:00:05,710
in that mysterious explosion
the other day...

4
00:00:05,710 --> 00:00:06,340
BREAKING NEWS: SUBSTANTIAL DONATION
TOWARD THE STADIUM'S RESTORATION

5
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:07,500
but there appear
to have been a new development.

6
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:08,340
REPRESENTATIVE MORIO KOUDA

7
00:00:08,340 --> 00:00:10,800
You may remember
Representative Morio Kouda...

8
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:13,930
who recently made headlines
over illegal campaign contributions.

9
00:00:14,470 --> 00:00:17,850
According to sources close to the matter,
his support group has offered...

10
00:00:17,850 --> 00:00:20,390
to make a substantial donation
toward the stadium's restoration.

11
00:00:20,390 --> 00:00:23,270
I'd like to discuss this.

12
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:27,650
Of course I was worried.

13
00:00:27,650 --> 00:00:30,030
But more importantly,
is that story really true?

14
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:34,990
When Ogami and you found
the kidnappers' car...

15
00:00:34,990 --> 00:00:38,030
they started playing catch
in the park to blow off some steam.

16
00:00:38,030 --> 00:00:41,120
And then you two rescued Noren
while the kidnappers were distracted?

17
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:42,790
Dead serious.

18
00:00:43,210 --> 00:00:46,500
What kind of kidnappers do that?

19
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:49,840
Never mind that. You were
that worried about me, Chisato?

20
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:51,340
Could it be that you—

21
00:00:51,340 --> 00:00:53,510
I was just worried. That's all.

22
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:54,880
Huh?

23
00:02:33,980 --> 00:02:36,110
Mornin', Oga!

24
00:02:36,110 --> 00:02:36,990
Mornin'!

25
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:38,990
Morning.

26
00:02:38,990 --> 00:02:39,280
MODERN MIDDLE SCHOOL
JAPANESE LITERATURE 1

27
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:40,270
Your face is freaking me out!

28
00:02:40,270 --> 00:02:42,030
Whoa! What's going on?

29
00:02:42,030 --> 00:02:44,080
It isn't even time for finals yet!

30
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,950
Don't mind me.

31
00:02:45,950 --> 00:02:49,580
It's been a while, so I'm trying
to focus on getting to school.

32
00:02:49,870 --> 00:02:52,170
What do you mean
by "focus on getting to school"?

33
00:02:52,170 --> 00:02:54,460
"Been a while"?
We just had a normal weekend!

34
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:56,050
What's wrong, Oga?

35
00:02:56,710 --> 00:02:58,680
Maybe he's excited to see her.

36
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:02,140
Sorry.

37
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:03,640
I'm gonna go on ahead.

38
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:04,810
Uh, sure.

39
00:03:05,270 --> 00:03:06,270
Boss?

40
00:03:06,270 --> 00:03:08,350
Noren's just past the shoe cubbies.

41
00:03:08,350 --> 00:03:09,230
Huh?

42
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:12,440
Whoa! With your level, you really
can sense people's presence, and—

43
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:13,060
No.

44
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:17,150
I can see that weird little
springy hair of hers sticking out.

45
00:03:17,150 --> 00:03:20,320
Oh, crap! You're right!
Even an idiot could've spotted that!

46
00:03:25,490 --> 00:03:27,910
What am I even doing?

47
00:03:27,910 --> 00:03:30,420
Lurking here like I'm lying in wait...

48
00:03:30,420 --> 00:03:34,960
But I just can't stop
thinking about Ogami!

49
00:03:35,250 --> 00:03:36,630
Sorry, Noren.

50
00:03:36,630 --> 00:03:40,220
Those aren't your real feelings.
It's the hypnosis talking.

51
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:44,600
But if this turns into some weird
situation we can't take back,

52
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:47,970
then snapping her out of it
won't be enough.

53
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:52,020
So, I'm gonna keep my distance
for a while.

54
00:03:58,110 --> 00:03:59,860
Master! Good morning!

55
00:04:00,610 --> 00:04:02,530
Morning, Ogami!

56
00:04:02,530 --> 00:04:03,450
And...

57
00:04:03,450 --> 00:04:06,330
how many times have I asked you
to stop calling me "Master"?

58
00:04:06,870 --> 00:04:09,540
Maybe this will help.

59
00:04:10,160 --> 00:04:11,540
- You're banished.
- Why?

60
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:18,710
I heard you went on a double date.

61
00:04:19,090 --> 00:04:22,300
- With my sister and that Young Corn guy.
- Well... Uh... I mean...

62
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:23,300
Unicorn.

63
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:25,140
Same difference.

64
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:29,100
You sided with the bug buzzing
around my sister? What's that about?

65
00:04:29,100 --> 00:04:29,850
Sorry, sir!

66
00:04:32,770 --> 00:04:34,190
Oh, there you are!

67
00:04:34,190 --> 00:04:35,690
Morning, Shiraishi!

68
00:04:36,020 --> 00:04:36,730
Mornin'!

69
00:04:36,730 --> 00:04:37,360
Huh?

70
00:04:37,730 --> 00:04:39,030
And...

71
00:04:39,030 --> 00:04:40,860
good morning, Ogami.

72
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:43,740
Good morning! I, uh, have to poop!

73
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:48,910
"Good morning! I, uh, have to poop!"

74
00:04:48,910 --> 00:04:49,910
What?

75
00:04:49,910 --> 00:04:52,250
That's how a grade-schooler
runs away, old man!

76
00:04:52,790 --> 00:04:56,170
So, yeah, that's where
the boss is at right now.

77
00:04:58,960 --> 00:05:00,380
My stomach hurts!

78
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:03,090
This isn't funny, y'know.

79
00:05:03,090 --> 00:05:05,260
The double date was a whole mess, too!

80
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:07,970
Nope, can't do it!

81
00:05:07,970 --> 00:05:09,510
I'm laughing so much...

82
00:05:09,850 --> 00:05:12,060
I can't finish my coffee!

83
00:05:12,060 --> 00:05:12,980
Eri...

84
00:05:14,100 --> 00:05:15,690
Sorry, sorry!

85
00:05:16,230 --> 00:05:17,270
So...

86
00:05:17,270 --> 00:05:20,940
the real issue is that he suddenly changed
back into his original body, right?

87
00:05:20,940 --> 00:05:22,150
Right.

88
00:05:22,150 --> 00:05:23,240
Hm...

89
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:26,410
Then we need to pin down the cause
as soon as possible.

90
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:28,910
If he turns back into
his middle-aged self during class,

91
00:05:28,910 --> 00:05:30,330
that's not exactly comedy material.

92
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:31,830
There's some old guy in here?

93
00:05:31,830 --> 00:05:32,750
Who is it?

94
00:05:33,330 --> 00:05:34,410
Exactly!

95
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:37,630
Did he eat something that had gone bad?

96
00:05:37,630 --> 00:05:39,920
He didn't get food poisoning.

97
00:05:40,500 --> 00:05:42,460
I was half-joking.

98
00:05:42,460 --> 00:05:44,340
But the most likely
possibility is still...

99
00:05:44,340 --> 00:05:47,930
that he ingested something
and it triggered a reaction.

100
00:05:47,930 --> 00:05:49,220
If the poison had simply worn off...

101
00:05:49,220 --> 00:05:51,180
he wouldn't have turned
back into a kid afterward.

102
00:05:51,890 --> 00:05:56,940
So, first, can you go back and check
everything he put in his mouth that day?

103
00:05:57,230 --> 00:05:58,560
Got it!

104
00:05:58,980 --> 00:06:02,400
Also, you said he tangled
with some JARDIN assassins?

105
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:03,570
Oh, yeah.

106
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:05,530
Here's the thing.

107
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:09,160
Mitsuoka's wasps
were artificially created.

108
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:09,780
So...

109
00:06:10,070 --> 00:06:12,200
the fastest way to get answers would be...

110
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:15,370
to find whoever made them and 
squeeze the information out of that person.

111
00:06:15,370 --> 00:06:18,080
But that kind of information is top secret.

112
00:06:18,670 --> 00:06:19,750
And yet, somehow...

113
00:06:20,210 --> 00:06:23,250
JARDIN seems to have gotten their hands
on some of it.

114
00:06:34,810 --> 00:06:36,810
SCHOOL NEWSPAPER

115
00:07:27,900 --> 00:07:30,490
Oga, we need to talk to you for a sec.

116
00:07:30,860 --> 00:07:31,820
Hm?

117
00:07:32,530 --> 00:07:34,240
Sorry, man.

118
00:07:34,490 --> 00:07:35,830
Huh? Hey!

119
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:39,960
See, we received a little request
to take you into custody.

120
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:41,460
In exchange for convenience-store pudding.

121
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:44,000
- That cheap?
- Can you guess who our client is?

122
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:49,340
Ogami! What is going on?
You're acting so weird today!

123
00:07:49,340 --> 00:07:51,880
You're the one acting weird, Noren!

124
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:54,220
Why are you avoiding me?

125
00:07:54,220 --> 00:07:55,640
I just...

126
00:07:55,640 --> 00:07:56,720
Forget it!

127
00:07:57,010 --> 00:07:59,350
I can't take it anymore!
I can't hold it in!

128
00:07:59,640 --> 00:08:00,980
Huh? Wait, is this...

129
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:02,190
No way! For real?

130
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:04,440
I don't care about the situation!

131
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:06,190
You sure now's the time, Noren?

132
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:08,900
I... I think I lo—

133
00:08:09,190 --> 00:08:11,280
I screwed up royally!

134
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:14,450
I avoided her way too obviously,
and now Noren's gone berserk?

135
00:08:18,950 --> 00:08:20,960
Let's talk about this some other time!

136
00:08:20,960 --> 00:08:21,620
Hey!

137
00:08:22,750 --> 00:08:24,630
Wait, Ogami!

138
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:28,050
Come on, listen to me!

139
00:08:28,500 --> 00:08:30,300
S-So fast!

140
00:08:30,630 --> 00:08:33,430
She's not an all-rounder for nothing!

141
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,860
You've gotta be kidding me!

142
00:08:54,860 --> 00:08:56,870
She's seriously chasing me?

143
00:08:56,870 --> 00:08:58,740
Noren is fast!

144
00:09:30,980 --> 00:09:32,690
Oh! There he is!

145
00:09:32,690 --> 00:09:33,690
Ogami!

146
00:09:34,900 --> 00:09:36,860
Looks like I finally shook her.

147
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:42,660
No helping it. I'll just go home for today
and come back for my bag later.

148
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,500
RIKKA MIDDLE SCHOOL VOLLEYBALL TEAM

149
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:47,750
Excuse me! Can I borrow that for a second?

150
00:09:47,750 --> 00:09:48,380
Huh?

151
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:49,630
Wait!

152
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:50,630
Huh?

153
00:09:50,630 --> 00:09:52,090
RIKKA MIDDLE SCHOOL

154
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:54,920
RIKKA MIDDLE SCHOOL VOLLEYBALL TEAM

155
00:10:00,640 --> 00:10:02,600
I like you, Ogami!

156
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:04,520
And if you're still going to run away,
then game on!

157
00:10:05,100 --> 00:10:08,100
If I catch you,
you have to go out with me!

158
00:10:08,100 --> 00:10:09,520
Not pretend! For real!

159
00:10:09,940 --> 00:10:11,860
She's cooler than any assassin!

160
00:10:11,860 --> 00:10:14,650
No, wait, wrong reaction!
How the hell did we get here?

161
00:10:14,650 --> 00:10:17,030
Noren, what's gotten into you?

162
00:10:17,030 --> 00:10:21,030
SATURDAY, JUNE 13th

163
00:10:22,530 --> 00:10:23,700
RIKKA MIDDLE SCHOOL

164
00:10:24,660 --> 00:10:26,000
RIKKA MIDDLE SCHOOL VOLLEYBALL CLUB

165
00:10:31,340 --> 00:10:33,300
I like you, Ogami!

166
00:10:33,300 --> 00:10:35,300
And if you're still going to run away,
then game on!

167
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:38,720
If I catch you,
you have to go out with me!

168
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:40,300
Not pretend! For real!

169
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:42,260
How the hell did we get here?

170
00:10:42,260 --> 00:10:43,890
Noren, what's gotten into you?

171
00:10:44,270 --> 00:10:45,310
What's going on?

172
00:10:45,310 --> 00:10:47,140
Aren't those two a couple?

173
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:48,810
Lovers' spat?

174
00:10:48,810 --> 00:10:50,150
Romantic drama?

175
00:10:50,150 --> 00:10:52,940
This is bad.
People are starting to gather.

176
00:10:52,940 --> 00:10:56,490
<i>And a rampaging Noren
is completely unpredictable!</i>

177
00:10:56,490 --> 00:10:58,900
Okay! Let's just go
somewhere else and talk.

178
00:11:04,540 --> 00:11:06,410
Let's calm down and talk this through.

179
00:11:06,410 --> 00:11:12,250
We were only fake dating as a joke
to keep guys from hitting on you, right?

180
00:11:12,250 --> 00:11:17,630
We were, but I really did f-fall for you!

181
00:11:17,630 --> 00:11:22,220
I don't even know why, but I can't
hold these feelings back anymore!

182
00:11:22,890 --> 00:11:24,310
Dammit!

183
00:11:24,310 --> 00:11:27,480
Kazuma's hypnosis really got its hooks in.

184
00:11:27,810 --> 00:11:29,350
No, wait.

185
00:11:32,230 --> 00:11:33,360
Sorry.

186
00:11:34,650 --> 00:11:38,690
I can't see you that way, Mitsuoka.

187
00:11:38,690 --> 00:11:41,110
The most I can do is keep pretending.

188
00:11:41,410 --> 00:11:44,910
If running away and avoiding her
just makes this whole thing messier,

189
00:11:44,910 --> 00:11:47,370
then I'm better off
turning her down straight.

190
00:11:47,370 --> 00:11:49,870
I should've done this from the start, maybe.

191
00:11:49,870 --> 00:11:51,120
Oh...

192
00:11:51,920 --> 00:11:53,540
Okay.

193
00:11:53,540 --> 00:11:55,590
Yeah. I get it.

194
00:11:55,590 --> 00:11:57,960
Sorry for making such a scene.

195
00:12:04,260 --> 00:12:05,760
Then I'll die.

196
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:07,810
Hold it, hey!

197
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:09,980
Wait, wait, wait, calm down!

198
00:12:09,980 --> 00:12:12,520
How is that your answer?
Get back here! It's dangerous!

199
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:13,690
Let go of me!

200
00:12:13,690 --> 00:12:16,940
What's the point of living
in a world without you in it, Ogami?

201
00:12:16,940 --> 00:12:19,570
I'm in it! No, that's not the point!
Don't do anything stupid!

202
00:12:19,570 --> 00:12:21,320
And also, isn't that kind of unfair?

203
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:24,990
You've turned guys down tons of times, 
but the second you confess and get rejected,

204
00:12:24,990 --> 00:12:26,410
you jump straight to dying?

205
00:12:26,410 --> 00:12:27,870
That's so mean!

206
00:12:27,870 --> 00:12:30,790
Okay, yeah, maybe this wasn't
the time to bring that up!

207
00:12:44,390 --> 00:12:46,100
I started suspecting it along the way,

208
00:12:46,100 --> 00:12:49,430
but something is seriously off
with this version of Noren.

209
00:12:49,430 --> 00:12:52,560
Is this what she's like when she falls
for somebody 100% for real?

210
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:57,440
I mean, I've never seen her
around someone she actually likes.

211
00:12:57,440 --> 00:13:00,030
Only the man-hating side.

212
00:13:00,030 --> 00:13:01,280
But still...

213
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:04,280
Can someone's whole character 
change this much?

214
00:13:06,570 --> 00:13:08,410
A call from an unknown number?

215
00:13:08,950 --> 00:13:10,080
No!

216
00:13:10,740 --> 00:13:12,450
It's the same number as before!

217
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:14,460
Which means...

218
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:15,330
CHINATOWN

219
00:13:15,330 --> 00:13:17,170
Hello? Kazuma?

220
00:13:17,170 --> 00:13:18,380
Indeed.

221
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:20,340
So? How are things on your end?

222
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:23,380
Noren, sorry, I need to take this!

223
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:25,510
Uh, dying is bad, okay? Hold on!

224
00:13:27,260 --> 00:13:29,050
How do you think things are?

225
00:13:29,050 --> 00:13:32,770
I'll give you credit for calling at the
perfect time, but something's wrong here!

226
00:13:32,770 --> 00:13:34,980
What kind of hypnosis
did you put on Noren?

227
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:36,350
I told you, didn't I?

228
00:13:36,350 --> 00:13:39,610
When she wakes, she will fall in love
with the first person she sees.

229
00:13:39,610 --> 00:13:41,110
Deeply.

230
00:13:41,980 --> 00:13:44,780
I can't live without you, Ogami!

231
00:13:44,780 --> 00:13:47,620
Hey! You left that last part out!
Was that necessary?

232
00:13:47,990 --> 00:13:51,080
What the hell does that even mean?
Why would you add that extra crap?

233
00:13:51,080 --> 00:13:54,330
My younger brother mentioned
that he's not fond of flighty girls.

234
00:13:54,330 --> 00:13:56,000
Are you screwing with me? Are you stupid?

235
00:13:56,330 --> 00:13:58,040
She wasn't flighty to begin with...

236
00:13:58,040 --> 00:14:01,250
so stop flooring the gas pedal
in the wrong direction!

237
00:14:01,250 --> 00:14:03,590
When the hell
are you guys transferring in?

238
00:14:03,590 --> 00:14:06,130
These injuries won't heal in a day or two.

239
00:14:06,130 --> 00:14:07,800
It'll still be a while.

240
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:08,970
That's no good!

241
00:14:08,970 --> 00:14:11,600
I can't wait! Undo it right now!
I'm serious!

242
00:14:12,390 --> 00:14:14,020
Very well.

243
00:14:14,680 --> 00:14:16,440
Meet me at five o'clock.

244
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:18,440
Bring Noren Mitsuoka with you.

245
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:19,520
The location is...

246
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:23,900
The two of us going out
to Yokohama together...

247
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:25,320
This is totally a date now, right?

248
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:26,360
Y-Yeah.

249
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:28,280
A date, or, uh, more like
a reverse-hypno appointment.

250
00:14:28,280 --> 00:14:28,910
COSMIC WORLD

251
00:14:28,910 --> 00:14:31,200
The meetup spot is an amusement park, too.

252
00:14:31,200 --> 00:14:34,160
Her thinking it's a date at least
made it easier to invite her.

253
00:14:34,450 --> 00:14:37,080
Hey, can we go to the Cup Noodle Museum?

254
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:38,580
Huh? Cup what museum?

255
00:14:39,580 --> 00:14:41,840
I've always wanted to come here!

256
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:43,550
Are we gonna make it in time?

257
00:14:45,050 --> 00:14:48,180
So, you eat cup ramen, too.

258
00:14:48,180 --> 00:14:50,800
I guess I never really
pictured you eating it.

259
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:53,060
I used to eat it with my uncle.

260
00:14:53,060 --> 00:14:54,890
It's so good!

261
00:14:55,180 --> 00:14:57,520
Whoa, look! Amazing!

262
00:14:57,520 --> 00:15:03,230
Natsukiya's fancy ramen is top-tier, but
cheap and easy cup noodles are great, too.

263
00:15:03,230 --> 00:15:04,780
- Cheap?
- Huh?

264
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:07,320
What do you mean, Ogami?

265
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:09,610
Cup ramen is a food
deeper than the deepest ocean,

266
00:15:09,610 --> 00:15:11,240
created through every kind of ingenuity...

267
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:13,450
to overcome the barriers
of production cost and shelf life!

268
00:15:13,450 --> 00:15:16,750
Cup ramen only reached this point because
our predecessors researched day and night

269
00:15:16,750 --> 00:15:19,330
to help people
suffering from food shortages.

270
00:15:19,330 --> 00:15:20,870
I really don't think
you can sum all that up...

271
00:15:20,870 --> 00:15:22,920
with a simple phrase
like "cheap and easy"!

272
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:24,800
Oh, crap! I stepped on a land mine!

273
00:15:25,090 --> 00:15:28,050
Come on! We're doing the history section
first, and we're doing it properly.

274
00:15:28,050 --> 00:15:29,550
I'll handle the commentary!

275
00:15:29,840 --> 00:15:30,800
Yes, ma'am.

276
00:15:31,800 --> 00:15:33,800
THE GRAND HISTORY OF CUP RAMEN

277
00:15:41,230 --> 00:15:42,770
Okay, we should probably get going.

278
00:15:43,110 --> 00:15:45,110
This is where the real fun starts!

279
00:15:45,110 --> 00:15:47,900
Now that we're here,
we have to make instant ramen!

280
00:15:50,530 --> 00:15:51,530
You don't want to?

281
00:15:51,530 --> 00:15:55,080
Let's make one-of-a-kind
instant noodles, Noren.

282
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:56,160
Okay!

283
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:58,540
Well, are we gonna make it in time?

284
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:03,710
Huh? From the dough?

285
00:16:03,710 --> 00:16:05,500
Th-That's enough!

286
00:16:05,500 --> 00:16:06,800
Stop, stop!

287
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:09,170
She's frying noodles
without even looking.

288
00:16:09,170 --> 00:16:12,470
At this point, she's basically
a noodle-frying master!

289
00:16:12,470 --> 00:16:15,720
Wait. Is she taking all of those home?

290
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:16,350
LOVE NOODLE

291
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:16,970
Ta-da!

292
00:16:17,930 --> 00:16:20,980
I can already feel that heavy dose
of love sitting in my stomach.

293
00:16:20,980 --> 00:16:26,570
But the meetup time's getting close, so
hey, it's good that she finished safely.

294
00:16:26,570 --> 00:16:28,980
Noren, there's somewhere
I want to go together—

295
00:16:30,820 --> 00:16:32,400
Wait, we're eating it now?

296
00:16:32,400 --> 00:16:34,530
Huh? After all, it's fresh.

297
00:16:34,530 --> 00:16:36,080
"After all"...

298
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:39,330
Crap! I've gotta scarf this down
and get us moving!

299
00:16:39,580 --> 00:16:44,170
So, I tried to express how I feel
about you right now, Ogami!

300
00:16:44,540 --> 00:16:45,790
Through spice!

301
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:52,800
Is this...

302
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:56,800
actually safe for human consumption?

303
00:16:57,100 --> 00:16:58,260
Enjoy!

304
00:17:00,350 --> 00:17:01,430
Enjoy!

305
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:04,400
Enjoy!

306
00:17:06,860 --> 00:17:08,270
Here goes.

307
00:17:14,820 --> 00:17:16,910
There's plenty more if you want seconds!

308
00:17:23,750 --> 00:17:25,620
I made it out alive.

309
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,130
The meeting place
should be around here, right?

310
00:17:30,130 --> 00:17:32,010
Did we make it just in time?

311
00:17:32,460 --> 00:17:34,300
Hey, Ogami!

312
00:17:34,630 --> 00:17:35,760
Let's ride that!

313
00:17:36,090 --> 00:17:38,680
Huh? We don't have time for rides!

314
00:17:38,680 --> 00:17:42,390
And if we get on the Ferris wheel, I'll be
stuck in an enclosed space with Noren!

315
00:17:44,350 --> 00:17:47,270
You don't want to? I knew it!
Someone like me could never—

316
00:17:47,270 --> 00:17:48,810
We'll ride it! We'll ride it, okay?

317
00:18:20,050 --> 00:18:22,100
Wow, look!

318
00:18:22,470 --> 00:18:24,680
And the sun's just about to set, too!

319
00:18:24,680 --> 00:18:26,230
Amazing!

320
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:28,060
Mitsuoka, it's dangerous to stand...

321
00:18:37,530 --> 00:18:40,700
O-Ogami...

322
00:18:44,950 --> 00:18:46,660
I knew this was a bad idea!

323
00:18:46,660 --> 00:18:49,370
I knew we should've skipped
the Ferris wheel!

324
00:18:49,370 --> 00:18:52,380
Don't do this, Noren! Don't close
your eyes like the mood is just right!

325
00:18:52,670 --> 00:18:55,050
I can't! I'm actually an old man!

326
00:18:55,050 --> 00:18:56,840
I've gotta turn this down! Huh?

327
00:18:57,130 --> 00:19:00,970
No, wait! If I reject her, this version
of Noren might try to die again!

328
00:19:00,970 --> 00:19:04,350
No, definitely! She almost spiraled
when I hesitated about the Ferris wheel!

329
00:19:04,350 --> 00:19:05,470
Okay, calm down!

330
00:19:05,470 --> 00:19:06,230
Huh?

331
00:19:06,230 --> 00:19:09,850
This is an old man and a first-year
middle school girl! Don't be a moron!

332
00:19:13,980 --> 00:19:17,030
If I don't kiss her here, Noren dies.

333
00:19:17,030 --> 00:19:18,110
Literally.

334
00:19:19,110 --> 00:19:21,410
If I do kiss her, I die.

335
00:19:21,410 --> 00:19:23,120
Socially.

336
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:25,370
Either way, I'm finished!

337
00:19:25,370 --> 00:19:26,120
No!

338
00:19:26,750 --> 00:19:28,960
Don't underestimate a legendary assassin!

339
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:34,290
Huh?

340
00:19:35,170 --> 00:19:36,760
No way! The door's open?

341
00:19:37,130 --> 00:19:40,760
I thought it was supposed to be locked
from the outside! What do we do?

342
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:44,010
Stay calm! We should be able
to call them on that intercom!

343
00:19:45,010 --> 00:19:47,770
I made the bullet ricochet
and broke the lock.

344
00:19:47,770 --> 00:19:50,060
She'll be scared until we get back down.

345
00:19:50,060 --> 00:19:52,270
Sorry, Noren. Hang in there.

346
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:55,820
Are you all right?

347
00:19:56,820 --> 00:19:58,440
That was so scary!

348
00:19:58,440 --> 00:20:00,900
We never thought
such an accident would happen!

349
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:02,660
We're terribly sorry!

350
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:05,830
Could you folks come with me
for a moment?

351
00:20:15,750 --> 00:20:17,000
Honestly...

352
00:20:17,500 --> 00:20:19,630
you're the one who rushed me.

353
00:20:19,630 --> 00:20:21,930
So, why were you off flirting
on the Ferris wheel?

354
00:20:21,930 --> 00:20:24,510
Because of your hypnosis! You caused this!

355
00:20:24,890 --> 00:20:28,390
I broke the spell on Noren Mitsuoka,
and the one I placed on you, as well.

356
00:20:28,390 --> 00:20:29,810
That settles everything, right?

357
00:20:30,100 --> 00:20:31,060
Yeah.

358
00:20:31,060 --> 00:20:33,770
But are you sure? Undoing mine, too?

359
00:20:33,770 --> 00:20:34,520
It matters not.

360
00:20:35,480 --> 00:20:38,730
Our last battle showed me
the difference in our abilities.

361
00:20:38,730 --> 00:20:42,400
If I cannot defeat you
whether you are hypnotized or not...

362
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:45,410
then I may as well release you
and be done with it.

363
00:20:45,780 --> 00:20:46,990
Farewell.

364
00:20:46,990 --> 00:20:49,490
Next time, we shall meet at school.

365
00:22:32,600 --> 00:22:33,680
Your change!

366
00:22:34,510 --> 00:22:35,140
ENGLISH VOCABULARY

367
00:22:35,140 --> 00:22:36,230
You awake?

368
00:22:36,690 --> 00:22:37,810
Then let's head home.

369
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:40,560
Huh? Ogami?

370
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:43,780
Why was I asleep here?

371
00:22:49,870 --> 00:22:52,660
Why am I in Yokohama?

372
00:22:52,660 --> 00:22:54,750
Why am I alone with you?

373
00:22:54,750 --> 00:22:59,420
Huh? I feel weirdly refreshed,
but I don't remember a thing.

374
00:22:59,420 --> 00:23:00,580
So, that's it.

375
00:23:00,580 --> 00:23:03,040
Well, for now, I'm just glad
she's okay, but...

376
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:07,880
Mitsuoka...

377
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:09,890
Huh?

378
00:23:10,340 --> 00:23:11,640
Do you like me?

379
00:23:12,050 --> 00:23:14,810
Huh? What's with that
all of a sudden? Gross!

380
00:23:14,810 --> 00:23:16,730
I mean, as a friend, sure.

381
00:23:17,100 --> 00:23:20,270
Wait, you don't mean anything
more than that, do you?

382
00:23:20,270 --> 00:23:24,400
Because if you do, sorry, but you know
I can't do that kind of thing, right?

383
00:23:27,900 --> 00:23:28,820
Huh?

384
00:23:28,820 --> 00:23:30,740
Why are you crying, Ogami?

385
00:23:30,740 --> 00:23:31,950
Ogami?

386
00:23:32,320 --> 00:23:33,660
Thank goodness!

387
00:23:33,660 --> 00:23:37,330
I've never been so happy
to be called "gross" in my life!

388
00:23:37,330 --> 00:23:40,040
What are you talking about? Are you okay?

